===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|membre}}, from {{der|en|fro|menbre}}, from {{der|en|la|membrum||limb, body part}}, from {{der|en|itc-pro|*memzrom}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*mḗms|*mḗms, *mēms-rom|flesh}}. Akin to {{cog|got|𐌼𐌹𐌼𐌶||meat, flesh}}, {{cog|gme-cgo|menus|sc=Latn}}.

Coexists with native {{m|en|limb}}, from {{m+|ang|lim||limb, joint, main branch}}. Mostly {{displaced|en|lith||limb, joint, member|nocap=1|sl=1}}, from {{m+|ang|liþ||limb, member, join, tip}}, which still survives in British dialect.

